  "repeats": [],
  "notes": [
   "The parts are the same as in step 1. Nothing was added or dropped.",
   "The page shows several set-ups (UNO to UNO, UNO to Nano, Mega to UNO, MKR1000 to UNO). I built the UNO programmer to UNO target one with old-style wiring: D13 to D13 (SCK), D12 to D12 (MISO), D11 to D11 (MOSI), programmer D10 to target RESET, 5V to 5V and GND to GND.",
   "The 10 \u00b5F capacitor goes between the programmer's RESET (positive, long leg) and GND. The catalogue's UNO card has no GND.2 position noted, so I used GND.2 for the capacitor and GND.1 for the GND wire. They are the same ground net.",
   "The images show no breadboard, so the capacitor legs go straight into the programmer's RESET and GND header sockets.",
   "The USB cable joins the programmer only. The UNO card has no USB port name, so I left that port null. The target is powered from the programmer over the 5V and GND wires.",
   "The optional status LEDs mentioned for the sketch are not listed or shown on the page, so I left them out."
  ]
 },
